AArch64 MP+caspal-i128+ldp
"CASPAL (0,0)->(1,2) on a 16-byte location vs an LSE2 LDP: CASP is single-copy atomic at 128 bits (Arm ARM B2.2.1), so no torn read"
{
__int128 x;
0:X4=x; 1:X4=x;
uint64_t 0:X0; uint64_t 0:X1; uint64_t 1:X7; uint64_t 1:X8;
}
 P0                      | P1             ;
 MOV X0,#0               | LDP X7,X8,[X4] ;
 MOV X1,#0               |                ;
 MOV X2,#1               |                ;
 MOV X3,#2               |                ;
 CASPAL X0,X1,X2,X3,[X4] |                ;
exists (1:X7=1 /\ 1:X8=0 \/ 1:X7=0 /\ 1:X8=2)
